# Combining and reversing parent links
#
# Two parent facts form a short family chain: a is the parent of b, and b of
# c. Two ordinary N3 rules play the part of SPARQL property paths: one
# follows two parent links in a row to derive that a is the grandparent of
# c, the other follows a link backwards to derive who has which parent.

@prefix : <http://example/> .

# The family chain
:a :parentOf :b .
:b :parentOf :c .

# A sequence path: a parent of a parent is a grandparent
{
    ?x :parentOf ?y .
    ?y :parentOf ?z
} => {
    ?x :grandparentOf ?z
} .

# An inverse path: the parent link read backwards
{
    ?x :parentOf ?y
} => {
    ?y :hasParent ?x
} .
